  "evidence": [
    "V127 creates seven gateway positions and one reserved native provider-renewal slot per exact owned group device/native parent. Gateway positions pin the gateway head/version.",
    "Actual concurrent claims saturate only their bounded kind; release compares the exact old request and cannot delete its successor.",
    "Current native security/access, device state and chat eligibility are required for new storage claims; metadata remains owned after offboarding/native purge.",
    "Actual real-time expiry permits reclamation with a fresh token. Worker cleanup skips locked expired rows, cannot see/delete live rows, and preserves all device/provider/gateway provenance.",
    "Actual archive restore retains original Matrix identity and operational coordinates without a new credential envelope.",
    "Typed mapping rejects malformed scope, slot, purpose, gateway position, precision, chronology and overflow. Exact claim readback and post-release verification are inside the same safe I/O boundary.",
    "Real writes roll back after malformed readback, cancellation, interruption and failed caller results. Failed release verification restores the original lease.",
    "Both SQL and typed adapters require caller-owned transactions/current admission; no hidden retry or network I/O."
  ],
